{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSTabBarViewModifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Rendering","type":"heading","anchor":"Rendering","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS 26 brings Liquid Glass, the new Apple look and feel which will prevent developers to define specific styles for some critical components like bars."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because today the OUDS tab bar relies on native component and is not designed from scratch, some elements will look different between iOS 26 and older versions:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"background color of tab bar can be changed for iOS lower than 26","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"background color of tab bar does not change since iOS 26"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"normal \/ unselected tab item color can be changed for both image and text only for iOS lower than 26","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"with iOS 26 no token of color are applied on unselected \/ normal tab item because only the image will be changed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and not the text making theme not readable in dark color scheme","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition the badges colors will be the same and cannot be changed (except with token definition). These particular badges do not rely on OUDS badge components.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Since","content":[{"type":